module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ULiftUnit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ClosedSubspaceIdealQuasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteTypeChartSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.VanishingSubspace

/-!
# Étale descent of membership in the ideal generated by global functions

Let `F` be an algebraic space, let `U` be an étale chart of `F` whose underlying scheme is
affine, and let `f₁, …, f_r` be global regular functions on `F`.  A regular function on `U`
which lies in the ideal `(f₁|_V, …, f_r|_V)` after restriction along the members of some étale
covering of `U` already lies in `(f₁|_U, …, f_r|_U)`.

More generally, for a sheaf of modules cartesian on affine charts and finitely many of its
global sections, a section over `U` lying étale-locally in the submodule they generate lies in
that submodule over `U`.

Consequently the sheaf of ideals generated by `f₁, …, f_r` — the local closure of the presheaf
of ideals `V ↦ (f₁|_V, …, f_r|_V)`, which is not itself a sheaf — has exactly those ideals as
its sections over the affine étale charts.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingPresheafIdeal`: the presheaf of ideals of `𝒪_F` generated on
  each chart by the restrictions of `f₁, …, f_r`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingIdealSheaf`: its local closure, a sheaf of ideals of `𝒪_F`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_finite_affine_faithfullyFlat_pi_of_mem_topology`: a covering
  sieve of an affine étale chart contains a finite family of affine étale charts whose chart
  restrictions are jointly faithfully flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_eval_of_mem_topology`: **étale descent of membership in the
  submodule generated by finitely many global sections**, over an affine étale chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_vanishingIdealAt_of_mem_topology`: **étale descent of membership
  in the ideal generated by finitely many global regular functions**, over an affine étale
  chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingIdealSheaf_obj_of_isAffine`: the sections of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingIdealSheaf` over an affine étale chart are the ideal
  generated by the restrictions of the functions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_vanishingIdealSheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_vanishingIdealSheaf`: **the sheaf of ideals
  generated by finitely many global regular functions is cartesian on affine charts, hence
  quasi-coherent**, with no hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_vanishingSubfunctor_eq`: **`V(f₁, …, f_r)` is a closed
  subspace of `X` whose defining ideal on every affine étale chart is the ideal generated by
  `f₁|_U, …, f_r|_U`**, with no hypothesis.  This is the form
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.vanishingSubfunctor_eq` is phrased for, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_vanishingSubfunctor_eq_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite` carried it
  as a hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The passage from a covering sieve to a jointly faithfully flat finite family of affine charts is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_finite_affine_etale_ofArrows_le` combined with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.faithfullyFlat_pi_appTop`, and the descent itself is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_span_of_forall_restrict_mem_span`, whose only geometric input is
the injectivity half of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts`.  For the structure
sheaf that half is the unconditional
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_unit`, so the ideal statement carries no
hypothesis at all.

The sheaf of ideals has to be built as a local closure rather than chartwise.  The presheaf
`V ↦ (f₁|_V, …, f_r|_V)` is a submodule of the underlying presheaf of `𝒪_F`, but membership in
it is not a local condition on the small étale site, so it is not a
`SheafOfModules.Submodule`; `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localClosure` adjoins the sections lying
locally in it, and the content of the descent statement is that over an affine chart nothing is
adjoined.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.scalarMultiplesSubsheaf` is the same construction for an arbitrary
ringed site whose structure sheaf receives a family of global scalars; it is not used here
because its chartwise span is taken over the products of the scalars with *all* sections, so
identifying it with the ideal of the family is an extra step at every use.

